  (footprint "MeetingHub-4-v3:Jack_3.5mm_3pole_THT_Horizontal" (layer "F.Cu")
    (tstamp b3887f94-7914-47a8-abc0-504913ed942e)
    (at 70 89 180)
    (descr "P2 (3.5 mm) 3-conductor audio jack, right-angle THROUGH-HOLE. Part: SHOU HAN / HANXIA HX PJ-320A-3P DIP, LCSC C17701689. Pad geometry from the LCSC/EasyEDA library data for C17701689 (uuid c718c744) and the manufacturer datasheet (szlcsc 76D2D42B). Terminals numbered 2 / 3 / 4 exactly as the datasheet: pin 3 = TIP (leaf-spring contact = mic on a CTIA Y-splitter mic plug); pins 2 and 4 = ring and sleeve, both wired to GND in this design so their order does not matter. Two 1.0 mm NPTH locating posts 6.0 mm apart. Barrel points -Y and overhangs the -Y board edge. On bring-up confirm pin 3 is the tip contact (insert a 3.5 mm plug, check continuity plug-tip to pin 3); if it is pin 4, swap the mic net onto pin 4 in the schematic.")
